NAME
     echo - write its arguments

SYNOPSIS
     echo [-n] [-e] [ARG...]

DESCRIPTION
     echo writes its arguments separated by spaces, with a newline at the
     end.

OPTIONS
     -n   no newline at the end
     -e   interpret \n, \t, \\ and the other escapes

SEE ALSO
     printf is a shell built-in, cat(1)
